The algorithm uses three nested loops. The outermost loop iterates through all possible intermediate vertices $k$. The middle loop iterates through all possible source vertices $i$. The innermost loop iterates through all possible destination vertices $j$. The order is crucial:
```
for k from 1 to V:
    for i from 1 to V:
        for j from 1 to V:
            dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])
```
